  "worked_solution": "Remember that in general, if a point $A$ has coordinates $({a}_{x},{a}_{y},{a}_{z}),$ then its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OA}=\u27e8{a}_{x},{a}_{y},{a}_{z}\u27e9.\n$$\n\nHere, the point $P$ has coordinates $(0,0,3),$ so its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =\u27e80,0,3\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe point $Q$ has coordinates $(0,-3,2),$ so its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =\u27e80,-3,2\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe point $R$ has coordinates $(0,4,3),$ so its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\u27e80,4,3\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
